{"authored" [{"question" "q-71230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${(u(t)f(t))}^{′}$ where $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 8 \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)={t}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n{(u(t)f(t))}^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})=2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u(t)f(t))}^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =2t[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 8 \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]+{t}^{2}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2t{e}^{t} \\\\ 16t \\\\ 2t{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{t}^{2}{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(2t+{t}^{2}){e}^{t} \\\\ 16t \\\\ (2t-{t}^{2}){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e765ed6ca51892a692aaca1144141d35f40653eddb185731c2f43172d515fb83" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71230" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71230" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}(1-{t}^{2}){e}^{t} \\\\ 8t \\\\ (t+{t}^{2}){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71230" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}(2t+{t}^{2}){e}^{t} \\\\ 16t \\\\ (2t-{t}^{2}){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71230" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}({t}^{2}+{t}^{3}){e}^{t} \\\\ 4t \\\\ {t}^{3}{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71230" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}3t{e}^{t} \\\\ -8t \\\\ -3t{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71230" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{3}{e}^{t} \\\\ -16t \\\\ -{t}^{3}{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(u)={e}^{u+1}\\,i+{e}^{2u}\\,j+\\frac{1}{e}\\,k$ and $u(t)=2{t}^{2}$ then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)=f′(u(t))u′(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({e}^{u+1})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({e}^{2u})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\frac{1}{e}\\,k \\\\  & ={e}^{u+1}\\,i+2{e}^{2u}\\,j+0\\,k \\\\  & ={e}^{u+1}\\,i+2{e}^{2t}\\,j \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2})=4t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & =f′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\ (f∘u)^{′}(t) & =({e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+2{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j)4t \\\\  & =4t{e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+8t{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e765ed6ca51892a692aaca1144141d35f40653eddb185731c2f43172d515fb83" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "4t{e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+8t{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "4t{e}^{t+1}\\,i+6t{e}^{2t}\\,j"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "4{e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i-8{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "t{e}^{2t+1}\\,i+2t{e}^{4t}\\,j"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "t{e}^{t+1}\\,i+2t{e}^{2t}\\,j"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $(f\\cdot g)^{′}(t)$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =20t\\,i-2t\\,j+(2+5t)\\,k \\\\ g(t) & ={t}^{3}\\,i+t\\,j+({t}^{2}+t)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the dot product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n(f\\cdot g)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(t)\\cdot g(t)+f(t)\\cdot {g}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(20t)\\,i-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2+5t)\\,k \\\\  & =20\\,i-2\\,j+5\\,k \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+t)\\,k \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}\\,i+j+(2t+1)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f\\cdot g)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(t)\\cdot g(t)+f(t)\\cdot {g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(20\\,i-2\\,j+5\\,k)\\cdot ({t}^{3}\\,i+t\\,j+({t}^{2}+t)\\,k)+(20t\\,i-2t\\,j+(2+5t)\\,k)\\cdot (3{t}^{2}\\,i+j+(2t+1)\\,k) \\\\  & =(20{t}^{3}-2t+5({t}^{2}+t))+(60{t}^{3}-2t+(2+5t)(2t+1)) \\\\  & =80{t}^{3}+15{t}^{2}+10t+2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "e765ed6ca51892a692aaca1144141d35f40653eddb185731c2f43172d515fb83" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32298" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/state.json" "file_sha256" "02aba40fc50cf16c9ab6e00205fba03003ccabb09c25850b4f5a62f5f60ac5a6" "basis" 1410 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14039776/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-32298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $(f\\cdot g)^{′}(t)$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =20t\\,i-2t\\,j+(2+5t)\\,k \\\\ g(t) & ={t}^{3}\\,i+t\\,j+({t}^{2}+t)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5d87de1407425aab1797b19962388c92b5fa1d448d9c55f4138b02be33e6ad0"} {"question" "q-32298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the dot product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n(f\\cdot g)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(t)\\cdot g(t)+f(t)\\cdot {g}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(20t)\\,i-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2+5t)\\,k \\\\  & =20\\,i-2\\,j+5\\,k \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+t)\\,k \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}\\,i+j+(2t+1)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f\\cdot g)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(t)\\cdot g(t)+f(t)\\cdot {g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(20\\,i-2\\,j+5\\,k)\\cdot ({t}^{3}\\,i+t\\,j+({t}^{2}+t)\\,k)+(20t\\,i-2t\\,j+(2+5t)\\,k)\\cdot (3{t}^{2}\\,i+j+(2t+1)\\,k) \\\\  & =(20{t}^{3}-2t+5({t}^{2}+t))+(60{t}^{3}-2t+(2+5t)(2t+1)) \\\\  & =80{t}^{3}+15{t}^{2}+10t+2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5d87de1407425aab1797b19962388c92b5fa1d448d9c55f4138b02be33e6ad0"} {"question" "q-32298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9aaeb90fd4a53fb37b66163cbc9be084c3db1424222f7d7d46b1d07889cf311"} {"question" "q-32298" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5d87de1407425aab1797b19962388c92b5fa1d448d9c55f4138b02be33e6ad0"} {"question" "q-32298" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "60{t}^{3}+15{t}^{2}+14t+2"] ["math" "60{t}^{3}+7{t}^{2}+10t+2"] ["math" "80{t}^{3}+11{t}^{2}+12t+2"] ["math" "80{t}^{3}+15{t}^{2}+10t+2"] ["math" "80{t}^{3}+6{t}^{2}+10t+2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5d87de1407425aab1797b19962388c92b5fa1d448d9c55f4138b02be33e6ad0"} {"question" "q-32298" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "80{t}^{3}+15{t}^{2}+10t+2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5d87de1407425aab1797b19962388c92b5fa1d448d9c55f4138b02be33e6ad0"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(u)={e}^{u+1}\\,i+{e}^{2u}\\,j+\\frac{1}{e}\\,k$ and $u(t)=2{t}^{2}$ then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5d87de1407425aab1797b19962388c92b5fa1d448d9c55f4138b02be33e6ad0"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)=f′(u(t))u′(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({e}^{u+1})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({e}^{2u})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\frac{1}{e}\\,k \\\\  & ={e}^{u+1}\\,i+2{e}^{2u}\\,j+0\\,k \\\\  & ={e}^{u+1}\\,i+2{e}^{2t}\\,j \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2})=4t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & =f′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\ (f∘u)^{′}(t) & =({e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+2{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j)4t \\\\  & =4t{e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+8t{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5d87de1407425aab1797b19962388c92b5fa1d448d9c55f4138b02be33e6ad0"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9aaeb90fd4a53fb37b66163cbc9be084c3db1424222f7d7d46b1d07889cf311"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5d87de1407425aab1797b19962388c92b5fa1d448d9c55f4138b02be33e6ad0"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "4t{e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+8t{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j"] ["math" "4t{e}^{t+1}\\,i+6t{e}^{2t}\\,j"] ["math" "4{e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i-8{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j"] ["math" "t{e}^{2t+1}\\,i+2t{e}^{4t}\\,j"] ["math" "t{e}^{t+1}\\,i+2t{e}^{2t}\\,j"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5d87de1407425aab1797b19962388c92b5fa1d448d9c55f4138b02be33e6ad0"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4t{e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+8t{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5d87de1407425aab1797b19962388c92b5fa1d448d9c55f4138b02be33e6ad0"} {"question" "q-71230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${(u(t)f(t))}^{′}$ where $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 8 \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)={t}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5d87de1407425aab1797b19962388c92b5fa1d448d9c55f4138b02be33e6ad0"} {"question" "q-71230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n{(u(t)f(t))}^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(8) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{-t})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})=2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u(t)f(t))}^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =2t[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 8 \\\\ {e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]+{t}^{2}[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2t{e}^{t} \\\\ 16t \\\\ 2t{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}{e}^{t} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{t}^{2}{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(2t+{t}^{2}){e}^{t} \\\\ 16t \\\\ (2t-{t}^{2}){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5d87de1407425aab1797b19962388c92b5fa1d448d9c55f4138b02be33e6ad0"} {"question" "q-71230" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9aaeb90fd4a53fb37b66163cbc9be084c3db1424222f7d7d46b1d07889cf311"} {"question" "q-71230" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5d87de1407425aab1797b19962388c92b5fa1d448d9c55f4138b02be33e6ad0"} {"question" "q-71230" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}(1-{t}^{2}){e}^{t} \\\\ 8t \\\\ (t+{t}^{2}){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}(2t+{t}^{2}){e}^{t} \\\\ 16t \\\\ (2t-{t}^{2}){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}({t}^{2}+{t}^{3}){e}^{t} \\\\ 4t \\\\ {t}^{3}{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3t{e}^{t} \\\\ -8t \\\\ -3t{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{3}{e}^{t} \\\\ -16t \\\\ -{t}^{3}{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5d87de1407425aab1797b19962388c92b5fa1d448d9c55f4138b02be33e6ad0"} {"question" "q-71230" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}(2t+{t}^{2}){e}^{t} \\\\ 16t \\\\ (2t-{t}^{2}){e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5d87de1407425aab1797b19962388c92b5fa1d448d9c55f4138b02be33e6ad0"} {"question" "q-128485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find  $(u(t)g(t))^{′}$ where $g(t)=⟨2{e}^{-t},\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,2⟩$ and $u(t)=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5d87de1407425aab1797b19962388c92b5fa1d448d9c55f4138b02be33e6ad0"} {"question" "q-128485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n(u(t)g(t))^{′}=u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${g}^{′}(t).$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{e}^{-t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2{e}^{-t},\\,\\frac{4}{t},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}) \\\\  & =t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)g(t))^{′} & =u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}⟨-2{e}^{-t},\\,\\frac{4}{t},\\,0⟩+t⟨2{e}^{-t},\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-{t}^{2}{e}^{-t},\\,2t,\\,0⟩+⟨2t{e}^{-t},\\,4t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,2t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t{e}^{-t}-{t}^{2}{e}^{-t},\\,2t+4t\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,2t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t{e}^{-t}(2-t),\\,2t(1+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,2t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5d87de1407425aab1797b19962388c92b5fa1d448d9c55f4138b02be33e6ad0"} {"question" "q-128485" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9aaeb90fd4a53fb37b66163cbc9be084c3db1424222f7d7d46b1d07889cf311"} {"question" "q-128485" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5d87de1407425aab1797b19962388c92b5fa1d448d9c55f4138b02be33e6ad0"} {"question" "q-128485" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨2-t,\\,2(1+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,t⟩"] ["math" "⟨t{e}^{-t}(2-t),\\,2t(1+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,2t⟩"] ["math" "⟨t{e}^{-t},\\,1+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,2t⟩"] ["math" "⟨{e}^{-t},\\,2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,2t-1⟩"] ["math" "⟨{t}^{2}{e}^{-t},\\,{t}^{2}(1+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,1⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5d87de1407425aab1797b19962388c92b5fa1d448d9c55f4138b02be33e6ad0"} {"question" "q-128485" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨t{e}^{-t}(2-t),\\,2t(1+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,2t⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5d87de1407425aab1797b19962388c92b5fa1d448d9c55f4138b02be33e6ad0"} {"question" "q-128572" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(u)=[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ {u}^{2} \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)={e}^{t}$, then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5d87de1407425aab1797b19962388c92b5fa1d448d9c55f4138b02be33e6ad0"} {"question" "q-128572" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the chain rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(u) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\,({u}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(6)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2u \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & =f′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2u(t) \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2({e}^{t}) \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {e}^{t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 2{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5d87de1407425aab1797b19962388c92b5fa1d448d9c55f4138b02be33e6ad0"} {"question" "q-128572" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9aaeb90fd4a53fb37b66163cbc9be084c3db1424222f7d7d46b1d07889cf311"} {"question" "q-128572" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "e5d87de1407425aab1797b19962388c92b5fa1d448d9c55f4138b02be33e6ad0"} {"question" "q-128572" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{alig